\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "confidence": 0.92}, "confidence": 0.92}, {"t_ms": 383662, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WvfSpRX12oSTNAC7iJnASV", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 383662, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WvfSpRX12oSTNAC7iJnASV", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 388862, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and pull request #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** The comment on `round_money` in `src/money.py` says it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), but the code used ROUND_HALF_UP. So `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I switched the rounding mode to ROUND_HALF_EVEN. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on commit 08d3cd5986 passed.\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check the requirement against its source. I went by the code comment and the test, which both say ROUND_HALF_EVEN.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_016hi7shMF4QMoWVw6qz2Huw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015GmzpfWbVFMzpXb8tV5ejH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01MsH4XZVknDsfQuXJqT5C2j", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212", "confidence": 0.7}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Sj4eZjkeTuC6rL7AtvWmEw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GXDpnCKeSWJnQ3u8gkX3dc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money, per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01U5NV9ALtTudmjeMnz1C2eX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-round-half-even", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-round-half-even-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018yWg27qD8HngZrkL5XQNSh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WvfSpRX12oSTNAC7iJnASV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-round-half-even", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "`round_money` in `src/money.py` said in its docstring that it used banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code actually passed `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Because of that, `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed and broke the nightly build (e.g. `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`).\n\nThis PR switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and pull request #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** The comment on `round_money` in `src/money.py` says it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), but the code used ROUND_HALF_UP. So `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I switched the rounding mode to ROUND_HALF_EVEN. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on commit 08d3cd5986 passed.\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check the requirement against its source. I went by the code comment and the test, which both say ROUND_HALF_EVEN.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}